# Line endings — one standard, shared verbatim by every Facturatix repository.
#
# The repository always stores LF. Each checkout gets its own platform's native ending, so a
# Windows working tree holds CRLF and a macOS or Linux one holds LF — and because git normalizes
# a working copy before it compares, neither ever surfaces as a modified file. Nobody has to
# configure anything: cloning is enough, on any operating system.
#
# Without this, the ending depends on each machine's `core.autocrlf`, and an editor that saves in
# the other convention rewrites whole files. A 35-line edit then ships as a 653-line diff, which
# buries the real change and makes `git blame` point at whoever last pressed save.
#
# Do NOT add `eol=` to the `*` rule below. Pinning a single ending for every platform is what
# leaves the checkout on the other platform permanently dirty — that is the failure this file
# exists to end, not a stricter version of it.
* text=auto

# ── Must be LF everywhere, Windows checkouts included ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are read by a Linux kernel inside a container or on a CI runner. A CR before the newline
# makes it look for an interpreter literally named `/bin/sh\r`, and the build fails with a message
# that names neither the file nor the reason.
*.sh              text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore     text eol=lf

# Emitted by tooling that writes LF and rewrites the file wholesale when it finds anything else.
pnpm-lock.yaml    text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# ── Explicit text, so one stray control byte cannot turn a source file binary ─────────────────
#
# `text=auto` decides by content: a single NUL anywhere in the first 8 KB makes git call the file
# binary, stop diffing it and skip normalization entirely. Naming the source extensions means a
# code file is always treated as code, and the damage shows up as a diff instead of hiding in one.
*.cs    text diff=csharp
*.ts    text
*.tsx   text
*.js    text
*.mjs   text
*.jsx   text
*.json  text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.md    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.sql   text
*.csproj text
*.props text
*.slnx  text
*.svg   text

# ── Binary assets, never normalized ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.snk   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
